# Review package: batch 8, slice rest

## 48bc45c6 Show where the link's encryption ends and whose agreement it rests on, warn before its certificate ends, and say that link names are public

Share access says whether the link is encrypted to this machine or to hornhoof.org, with a link to Let's Encrypt's Subscriber Agreement. The Machines tab warns the whole-company people 14 days before the link's certificate ends. Setup starts the link on a long random name instead of the company's name, and after it makes a link it waits up to 90 seconds for the certificate before it shows the link. SECURITY.md, the README and the public link guide say that names are public and how to turn the certificate off.

Two small components are new, LetsEncryptNote and LinkReady, so that Settings and Setup share the agreement line and Setup stays small.

Ruling: new files apps/web/src/ui/LetsEncryptNote.tsx and apps/web/src/ui/LinkReady.tsx, and TlsView in apps/web/src/types.ts - why: the agreement line is used by two screens and the certificate wait is a hook of its own - cost if wrong: two files to fold back into the screens
Ruling: SECURITY.md and guide/public-link.md lines placed by their text, not by line numbers, since plan 2 task 10 moved them - why: the brief says so - cost if wrong: a line in the wrong paragraph
Ruling: the Machines warning shows when expiresAt is less than 14 days away, including a certificate already past its date - why: it has not renewed either - cost if wrong: a stale warning after a renewal until the next visit to the tab

