CRAP 20.9 from before. It now decides whether an end counts, acceptEnd takes
it, endTyped sends a typed turn's end out, and typedEndError names how that
turn ended. Nothing changes in what they do.

The last commit's second ruling says both fakes wait for the stop's answer. It
is the three fakes for Claude Code, Codex and Kimi Code, read in their source
and seen with Kimi's, and real Kimi Code was not checked.

