## 216cd541 Fix flaky web waits: raise the Testing Library wait limit to 10 s

Testing Library findBy and waitFor give up after asyncUtilTimeout, one second by
default, while testTimeout is 20 s. On a loaded machine the first render of a
test can take longer than one second with no fault in the code; this showed in
AgentWindowCurrentTask.test.tsx (Unable to find role button name Task). A wait
ends as soon as its element appears, so the longer limit costs a healthy test
nothing. New direct test: an element that appears after 1.1 s is found.

Web suite before: 53.84 s, 769 tests. After: 54.69 s, 770 tests. No test in
apps/web expects a findBy or waitFor to fail (no rejects, no catch around them).

Ruling: limit is 10 s, half of testTimeout - why: a missing element still fails with a clear message before the 20 s test timeout - cost if wrong: a test that truly hangs fails 9 s later

